# <%= current_page.data.title %>

## Join Slack

Once you have your `hmcts.net` or `justice.gov.uk` email account, one of your team members can invite you to the HMCTS Slack workspace.

Most teams use the [hmcts-reform.slack.com](https://hmcts-reform.slack.com/) workspace.

After creating your account, update your Slack profile:

- set your full name
- add your team name and role to the "What I do" section

## Join common channels

Software engineers should join the [developers Slack channel](https://hmcts-reform.slack.com/messages/developers).

Your team lead should also add you to your team channels, including any team contact or build notices channels.

## GitHub to Slack mapping

After joining GitHub, add your user to the [Slack to GitHub mapping](https://github.com/hmcts/github-slack-user-mappings).

This lets Jenkins and other tools notify the right Slack user when they need to contact you about builds or pull requests.

## Troubleshooting

### I have a hmcts.net account and cannot sign up

This can happen if your Slack invite was approved but you have not been added to the SSO exclusion list.

Ask someone in your team to ask in the `#help-slack-hmcts` channel to check your account.
